==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈkɒk.ˌl/}}
* Rhymes: [[Rhymes:English:-ɒkəl|-ɒkəl]]

===Etymology 1===
From {{OF.}} ''[[cokille]]'' (French ''[[coquille]]''), from {{L.}} ''*cocchilia'', form of ''[[conchylia]]'', from {{AGr.}} '''{{polytonic|[[κογχύλιον]]}}''' (konkhylion), diminutive of '''{{polytonic|[[κογχύλη]]}}''' ‘mussel’.

====Noun====
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun}}

# Any of various [[edible]] [[European]] [[bivalve]] [[mollusk]]s, of the [[family]] ''[[Cardiidae]]'', having [[heart]]-[[shaped]] [[shell]]s.
# The shell of the cockle.
# A defect in sheepskin; firm dark nodules caused by the bites of [[ked]]s on live sheep
# (''plural'') One’s [[innermost]] [[feeling]]s (only in the expression “the cockles of one’s heart”).

